{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's shore\nA land of mystic beauty and honor to adore\nHere's an itinerary for thee to follow with care\nTo make thy trip a memorable one beyond compare\n\nDay the first in Tokyo's vibrant streets we shall roam\nVisit the famous Shibuya Crossing where crowds do throng\nNext to Meiji Shrine where ancient rituals are done\nThen to Asakusa's Senso-ji Temple where fortunes are won\n\nDay the second in Tokyo's Imperial Palace we shall stroll\nA majestic sight of grandeur and beauty to behold\nNext to Ueno Park where cherry blossoms bloom in spring\nAnd in the evening to Akihabara's neon lights we shall cling\n\nDay the third to Nikko's Toshogu Shrine we shall make our way\nA UNESCO World Heritage Site of grandeur and display\nNext to Lake Chuzenji where waterfalls cascade and play\nAnd in the evening to a traditional ryokan we shall stay\n\nDay the fourth to Kyoto's Fushimi Inari Shrine we shall ascend\nA thousand vermilion gates that rise like a phoenix to amend\nNext to Kinkaku-ji Temple where golden leaves do shine\nAnd in the evening to Gion's geisha district we shall divine\n\nDay the fifth to Nara's Todaiji Temple we shall journey on\nWhere the Great Buddha statue doth sit in majesty and throne\nNext to Nara Park where friendly deer do roam and play\nAnd in the evening to a traditional Japanese inn we shall stay\n\nDay the sixth to Hiroshima's Peace Memorial Park we shall stray\nA somber reminder of war's devastation and dismay\nNext to Miyajima Island where the Itsukushima Shrine doth float\nAnd in the evening to a local izakaya we shall toast\n\nDay the seventh to Osaka's Universal Studios we shall make our way\nA theme park of wonder and magic to display\nNext to Osaka Castle where history and legend do unfold\nAnd in the evening to a local restaurant we shall dine and be told\n\nThus ends thy journey to